            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Economic Policies</strong><br>\nHis economic policies, termed the \"War on Poverty,\" significantly reduced the national poverty rate. He implemented tax cuts and government spending to stimulate economic growth.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Not Seeking Re-election</strong><br>\nIn March 1968, Johnson shocked the nation by announcing he would not seek re-election, largely due to criticism over the Vietnam War and concern for his health.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Post-Presidency and Death</strong><br>\nAfter leaving office in 1969, Johnson retired to his Texas ranch, where he wrote his memoirs and reflected on his presidency until his death on January 22, 1973.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
